ing and associates with a component of the SWI/SNF chromatin remodelling complex.[provided by RefSeq, Jun 2011].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9NSI6","text":"May be a transcriptional activator. May be involved in chromatin remodeling (By similarity). Required for regulation of cell morphology and cytoskeletal organization (PubMed:21834987)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}